1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--modified-input","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/modified-input","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/modified-input","sourceHash":"1d3bb67942bb8f4e0c5b85d2ef61952014e74c001600fac49c0cb9c2c84360ce","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:22.975Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Modified Input","zh":"调整后的输入"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Modified input is language that has been adjusted to be more understandable for learners. It can be simplified (using easier words and shorter sentences), slowed down, or accompanied by extra context (visuals, gestures, repetition).","zh":"调整后的输入是指经过调整、让学习者更容易理解的语言。它可以经过简化（使用更简单的词语和更短的句子）、放慢语速，或辅以额外的语境信息（画面、手势、重复）。"}},{"id":"examples","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Examples","zh":"示例"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"A teacher speaking slowly and clearly to a class","zh":"老师面对全班缓慢而清晰地讲话"},{"en":"Comprehensible input YouTube channels that use limited vocabulary and visual aids","zh":"使用有限词汇和视觉辅助内容的可理解输入类 YouTube 频道"},{"en":"Graded readers that use controlled vocabulary","zh":"使用受控词汇编写的分级读物"},{"en":"A native speaker adjusting their speech when talking to a learner (\"foreigner talk\")","zh":"母语者与学习者交谈时调整自己的说话方式（“外国人话语”）"}]},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"/roadmap/library/beginner-level-content\">Beginner-Level Content</a>","zh":"<a href=\"/roadmap/library/beginner-level-content\">初级内容</a>"}},{"id":"how-it-fits-in","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How It Fits In","zh":"它在学习过程中的作用"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Modified input is most useful in Phase 1, when your vocabulary is too small to understand authentic native content. As your level increases, you transition from modified input to authentic input made comprehensible through tools (subtitles, dictionaries) rather than through simplification.","zh":"调整后的输入在阶段 1 最为有用，因为此时你的词汇量还不足以理解真实的母语内容。随着水平提高，你会从调整后的输入逐步过渡到真实输入；这些真实输入不是通过简化，而是借助字幕、词典等工具变得可理解。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The goal is always to move toward authentic content as quickly as possible. Modified input is a stepping stone, not a destination.","zh":"目标始终是尽快转向真实内容。调整后的输入只是一块垫脚石，而不是终点。"}},{"id":"optimal-input","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Optimal Input","zh":"最佳输入"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Another concept that crops up is \"Optimal Input\" for language learning. It's very related to Modified Input, and I already made a video on it, so here it is:","zh":"语言学习中还常会出现另一个概念——“最佳输入”。它与调整后的输入密切相关，而我已经为此制作过一期视频，请看："}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Modified input is justified by the comprehensible input principle (<a href=\"https://www.sdkrashen.com/content/books/principles_and_practice.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Krashen, 1982</a>): learners can only acquire language from input they understand. At the absolute beginner stage, unmodified native content is incomprehensible, so simplification — limited vocabulary, slower speech, visual support — makes initial exposure comprehensible and useful.","zh":"可理解输入原则（<a href=\"https://www.sdkrashen.com/content/books/principles_and_practice.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Krashen，1982</a>）为调整后的输入提供了理论依据：学习者只能从自己理解的输入中习得语言。在绝对初学者阶段，未经调整的母语内容无法理解，因此通过限定词汇、放慢语速和提供视觉辅助来简化内容，可以让最初接触到的输入变得可理解且有用。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Research by <a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Ferguson+1971+foreigner+talk+simplicity\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ferguson (1971, 1975)</a> on \"foreigner talk\" demonstrated that native speakers naturally simplify when speaking to non-native speakers, and that this simplified input supports early comprehension. Subsequent work confirmed that such input modifications — slower rate, clearer articulation, high-frequency vocabulary — are a natural and effective feature of early-stage language exposure.","zh":"<a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Ferguson+1971+foreigner+talk+simplicity\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ferguson（1971、1975）</a>对“外国人话语”的研究表明，母语者与非母语者交谈时会自然而然地简化语言，而这种简化后的输入有助于早期理解。后续研究证实，放慢语速、清晰发音和使用高频词汇等输入调整，是语言学习初期自然且有效的接触方式。"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"However, modified input is most effective as a bridge, not a permanent feature. <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/9780521568296\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Day &amp; Bamford (1998)</a> showed that learners benefit more from reading large amounts of slightly difficult authentic material than from heavily simplified texts, because authentic input develops the inferencing and contextual guessing skills that real-world comprehension demands. The goal is rapid progression to natural input — possibly made comprehensible through tools like subtitles and dictionaries — because this is the ultimate target.","zh":"不过，调整后的输入最适合充当桥梁，而不应成为永久性的学习方式。<a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/9780521568296\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Day &amp; Bamford（1998）</a>指出，与高度简化的文本相比，大量阅读略有难度的真实材料能让学习者获益更多，因为真实输入可以培养现实理解所需的推断能力和根据语境猜测的能力。目标是尽快过渡到自然输入——必要时可以借助字幕、词典等工具使其变得可理解——因为这才是最终目标。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
